#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179523 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "79e281dd-40c0-515a-a5d5-d063609ecf73" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to X"}] :question/id #uuid "30d54dcc-49a2-5cd0-9eb9-659413ed5c67" :question/math-academy-id "e-9525" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x,$ where $C=C_1 \\cup C_2$ is the path comprising of two line segments, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/assets/3d408de0d50e2688aa0b35d8af39b6847cfdf21d5ec583320f0204384304fbc8.png)" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x = x_2 - x_1,\n$$\n\nwhere $x_2$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and $x_1$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, $x_2 = -3$ and $x_1 = 3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x = x_2 - x_1 = (-3) - 3 = -6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179524 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6935944-0acd-5593-aa80-e56f6014c13f" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to Y"}] :question/id #uuid "d799bcde-dbf0-580e-921b-18e56d729ea1" :question/math-academy-id "e-9526" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y,$ where $C$ is the path along the semicircle of radius $3,$ traversed from the point $(3,0)$ to the point $(-3,0),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/assets/ca97546ecaf9e37bee53fcc2b0c66962cff67a91ee9b117cc8ac8531efa23efc.png)" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y = y_2 - y_1,\n$$\n\nwhere $y_2$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and $y_1$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, $y_2 = 0$ and $y_1 = 0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y = y_2 - y_1 =  0 - 0 = 0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179525 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fd19952-77af-5f27-a7ef-adf46b1958ae" :knowledge-point/title "Orientation-Dependence"}] :question/id #uuid "e1d24f1c-4b7c-5c5e-bf93-7f9e76dffdf2" :question/math-academy-id "e-9527" :question/problem "If $\\displaystyle\\int_{C} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x= 8$ and $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x= -2,$ calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x$ given that $C = C_1\\cup C_2.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C = C_1\\cup C_2$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x = -\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x$\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x = \\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x + \\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 8 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 8 & =-(-2)-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 8 & =2-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 6 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x = -6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179930 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "79e281dd-40c0-515a-a5d5-d063609ecf73" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to X"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b789fde0-58a5-5c55-b956-e0057d4c28b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177581} {:answer/id #uuid "d7406eac-1069-562a-9b51-334a25b31658" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177582} {:answer/id #uuid "459a4552-03f1-5246-a238-cf75556357c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177583} {:answer/id #uuid "593d5d3d-da4f-51ad-9337-06f5ade434f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177584} {:answer/id #uuid "5fba2df4-d484-5ca8-8f6b-9952975c217e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "459a4552-03f1-5246-a238-cf75556357c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177583} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f1569d0-cbe7-50fe-8502-26b1be81310c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177580}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c2ecd409-704d-58f0-912b-02eaced8c539" :question/math-academy-id "q-124146" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/assets/ac639fb08d54d2004aec96708ffd19bc080b028e739075687a84a09158cd4fd2.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along a semicircle of radius $2,$ traversed from the point $(2,1)$ to the point $(-2,1),$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${x}_{2}=-2$ and ${x}_{1}=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1}=(-2)-2=-4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179931 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "79e281dd-40c0-515a-a5d5-d063609ecf73" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to X"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6f6ee34-f05e-54b2-972a-260fe9a62700" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177587} {:answer/id #uuid "d795fdd5-c145-5b65-91ea-e8af7a3c0d59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177588} {:answer/id #uuid "d9aede5e-6769-534a-95e6-b42bb4bb550e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177589} {:answer/id #uuid "6380c0bd-2627-57a2-9733-9dfb90835def" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177590} {:answer/id #uuid "74ecef72-3f9d-5777-a639-db564f708419" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74ecef72-3f9d-5777-a639-db564f708419" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177591} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ec68575-c9c9-5d8b-b41c-3cb37ccc38ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177586}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9e083fe5-0dee-54d0-961d-f2a6d6581138" :question/math-academy-id "q-124147" :question/problem "Calculate ${∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the closed path along the unit circle, traversed once in the counterclockwise direction." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, the initial and terminal points are the same (since the path is closed and is traversed only once). Therefore, ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$ and we have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179932 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6935944-0acd-5593-aa80-e56f6014c13f" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to Y"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96eb707e-f747-5190-9ff5-ea6bb720485c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177593} {:answer/id #uuid "f9e76586-cb74-5d2d-b70e-9b8702f28de2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177594} {:answer/id #uuid "22d134e8-e186-5936-8f52-7b925c750c73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177595} {:answer/id #uuid "409f4869-f392-5b4e-acaf-da25a74c794a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177596} {:answer/id #uuid "7543f316-d6b3-5d25-a42f-749cf66c0abf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177597}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7543f316-d6b3-5d25-a42f-749cf66c0abf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177597} :answer-field/id #uuid "b74723ac-5d4b-591a-acdd-bd0f02c661e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177592}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "46935a1e-c060-58a7-ab7d-a527906c3000" :question/math-academy-id "q-124148" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/assets/2400f92070b4f7d4e0ad0309574b729da86754bc64b6d7a3c508433d1bbc7f76.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along the line segment between the points $(4,0)$ to the point $(0,3),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{2}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${y}_{1}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{2}=3$ and ${y}_{1}=0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1}=3-0=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179933 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fd19952-77af-5f27-a7ef-adf46b1958ae" :knowledge-point/title "Orientation-Dependence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ae8a9b2-24dd-5e92-9370-bb7f127ab808" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177599} {:answer/id #uuid "a9cf7bd9-341d-56b0-bfca-8c5fd6b6cfbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Impossible to determine" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177600} {:answer/id #uuid "16b5530d-6f41-50c8-a7cd-af6de855bf9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177601} {:answer/id #uuid "52c6136e-206e-5bd7-bad2-e4667b297427" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177602} {:answer/id #uuid "5d797af5-824b-5628-927a-323bcadbff01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16b5530d-6f41-50c8-a7cd-af6de855bf9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177601} :answer-field/id #uuid "db59d4c1-026e-5b1d-973f-c57f88c79f5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177598}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4dcfed6a-aece-5954-8f2d-d015ef026f97" :question/math-academy-id "q-124149" :question/problem "If ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=4$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=6,$ calculate ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4-6 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338321 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fd19952-77af-5f27-a7ef-adf46b1958ae" :knowledge-point/title "Orientation-Dependence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "415ade7c-5a79-5492-8a50-edeb6668ef2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Impossible to determine" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338323} {:answer/id #uuid "6c8ea61d-2dbd-596b-b490-02cd5e36e379" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338324} {:answer/id #uuid "124f71fe-c3d9-5275-a02a-e7bffd254773" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338325} {:answer/id #uuid "36787f21-988e-5c12-adf1-a110a30b1108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338326} {:answer/id #uuid "517cd13b-7ef6-5860-b60e-44c0abcc4846" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36787f21-988e-5c12-adf1-a110a30b1108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338326} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d8443e6-8d4d-5286-89ef-37939581c384" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "91767182-155c-5640-b85b-b94d940de243" :question/math-academy-id "q-124179" :question/problem "If ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=3$ and ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=5,$ calculate ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $y,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-3+5 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338328 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fd19952-77af-5f27-a7ef-adf46b1958ae" :knowledge-point/title "Orientation-Dependence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e69d300-5705-5fcf-b1de-4c07ba633fe6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Impossible to determine" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338330} {:answer/id #uuid "282f567c-0ece-5f24-9666-5bbc2f9fcebe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338331} {:answer/id #uuid "b468e567-6e72-5f10-b98c-dde5b71004ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338332} {:answer/id #uuid "bd450cd9-2ebd-5452-a140-d51507db6af9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338333} {:answer/id #uuid "25df5bd6-420d-5fd0-9bb8-9b15ace3391e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338334}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b468e567-6e72-5f10-b98c-dde5b71004ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338332} :answer-field/id #uuid "88dc27b0-eedd-577a-b021-18f792b98bf0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338329}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "af001433-c0f9-5747-83c1-c1b44c6bb72c" :question/math-academy-id "q-124182" :question/problem "If ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=14$ and ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=10,$ calculate ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-14+10 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338335 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fd19952-77af-5f27-a7ef-adf46b1958ae" :knowledge-point/title "Orientation-Dependence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98101b2a-4625-51d9-a16c-fa1179849be6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338337} {:answer/id #uuid "c985cb52-9b77-5923-beab-da521c4c994b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338338} {:answer/id #uuid "e8a26eac-1b7a-54ea-852f-0ff224e315a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338339} {:answer/id #uuid "edd27fcc-35c4-5dd3-874b-33a46999294e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338340} {:answer/id #uuid "ed97306d-fd56-5171-98ad-9ad3c5b752a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edd27fcc-35c4-5dd3-874b-33a46999294e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338340} :answer-field/id #uuid "b58d6835-b19a-5971-9689-ee5370f59999" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338336}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9112d4a6-0538-5dfd-b50f-816096433e40" :question/math-academy-id "q-124184" :question/problem "If ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=15$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=10,$ calculate ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 15 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 15 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x-10 \\\\ 25 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-25.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338342 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fd19952-77af-5f27-a7ef-adf46b1958ae" :knowledge-point/title "Orientation-Dependence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2eed2948-e090-52a8-a638-cdbacab19444" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338344} {:answer/id #uuid "d573aacd-1ee6-59e8-a75b-ab237da5aca0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338345} {:answer/id #uuid "cf731eef-7024-5581-b94b-26f1d1b3aa79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338346} {:answer/id #uuid "4d9a00ed-7e31-5d69-9e19-6140fd86d1cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338347} {:answer/id #uuid "ddd7d30a-f2af-5489-af28-197ec9399e52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d9a00ed-7e31-5d69-9e19-6140fd86d1cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338347} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2d98626-1adf-5275-86d1-338933831d8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338343}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4a21c32f-f27e-5b9a-abf8-82c6ab3d1449" :question/math-academy-id "q-124188" :question/problem "If ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=21,$ ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=2,$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-11,$ calculate ${\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -{\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & =2-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -21 & =2-(-11)+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -21 & =13+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -34 & ={\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-34.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338349 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "79e281dd-40c0-515a-a5d5-d063609ecf73" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to X"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d24840c5-5482-5370-b5ef-5cf1656cf66f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338351} {:answer/id #uuid "45475d22-71dc-5720-bbea-210ffe9ac584" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338352} {:answer/id #uuid "8d61e85f-6368-5277-b79c-b1edd206c064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338353} {:answer/id #uuid "0f0ef7a1-018b-5509-b216-fabac4d56d79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338354} {:answer/id #uuid "9b0dafbd-70a6-561b-8df7-595946a669d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d61e85f-6368-5277-b79c-b1edd206c064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338353} :answer-field/id #uuid "21b88802-bdec-560f-83a7-e2c0eb4ffd52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bdb117eb-94c5-5aa6-84e3-cccfaff59f91" :question/math-academy-id "q-124281" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/assets/6b095a29b433107c37cd7e28c853d9d3d3547fb64a9e874783206b86c0aca6c1.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along a quarter circle of radius $3,$ traversed from the point $(1,-3)$ to the point $(4,0),$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${x}_{2}=4$ and ${x}_{1}=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1}=4-1=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338356 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "79e281dd-40c0-515a-a5d5-d063609ecf73" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to X"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf1b1979-dcc1-5661-b53e-db7ad8a5251c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338358} {:answer/id #uuid "42391f1b-7b6c-55f8-864c-e03a9ea77941" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338359} {:answer/id #uuid "2407c22b-ba51-5eba-b3f3-3c75237585fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338360} {:answer/id #uuid "fb6d2ddb-d95d-561f-b7ad-f64289019875" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338361} {:answer/id #uuid "4e5b84c7-a7c5-5941-aeaa-0532b29c7bd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\pi -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2407c22b-ba51-5eba-b3f3-3c75237585fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338360} :answer-field/id #uuid "97599255-8ac6-5ad9-9d61-ccc40ed66762" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1adeb956-0ba5-5e0e-b5d3-deeb2bc5df1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-124325" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/assets/eaf6f930e6e28f4574587880fefbcf336a0cd2a03d9c5bf347440227f31dbdf7.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path comprising of a horizontal line segment of length $2$ and a semicircle of radius $4,$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${x}_{2}=-3$ and ${x}_{1}=7.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1}=(-3)-7=-10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338363 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "79e281dd-40c0-515a-a5d5-d063609ecf73" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to X"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "481ee16f-28f1-5b3f-998f-d45e5403ea13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338365} {:answer/id #uuid "28137e25-cb44-5724-bbd5-5463e27b3fe9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi +4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338366} {:answer/id #uuid "d3fbf2da-6eaa-5ad2-a9b1-76f26d7b0bc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338367} {:answer/id #uuid "d5def2eb-3eda-5e20-9946-156cdb92b4ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi +2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338368} {:answer/id #uuid "733efb5f-4272-54fb-a31d-5c97d566b0f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "733efb5f-4272-54fb-a31d-5c97d566b0f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338369} :answer-field/id #uuid "f89475e6-9b2f-52e6-a186-862e0a872d1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338364}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "476f9520-b66e-50cc-a390-72a7b7b1be70" :question/math-academy-id "q-124331" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/assets/e8eb38cc8230a86e7cb9970effea188d1375ea39808467eace9554d023797e5f.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the closed path along the circular segment of radius $4,$ traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, the initial and terminal points are the same (since the path is closed and is traversed only once). Therefore, ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$ and we have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338370 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6935944-0acd-5593-aa80-e56f6014c13f" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to Y"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1da63246-e969-549d-bb59-c872859279e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338372} {:answer/id #uuid "20003edb-35ea-5340-a1ef-8c445f426b6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5+5\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338373} {:answer/id #uuid "134add11-a8ac-5c4e-9ec1-2b27132f8150" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338374} {:answer/id #uuid "f47a4ff8-4890-5f9b-8cca-959ecfcb7ad1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338375} {:answer/id #uuid "e1b3963f-e8cc-5f3a-87a4-eeca37685adf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338376}] :answer-field/correct {:a